WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.420
The wait for the trailer and title release
of the fourth Avengers movie nearly drove

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.080
the whole internet out of its mind.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.660
But now that it's out in the wild, it's raising
way more questions than it answers.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.200
Here are the biggest questions we're left
grappling with.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.180
For all its many characters from across the
Marvel Cinematic Universe, Infinity War was

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.960
ultimately a movie about Thanos.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.420
He set out on a genocidal mission, and at
the end, he won.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.420
What's next?

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.280
We all know that the Avengers have unfinished
business with the Mad Titan but what are Thanos'

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:29.780
plans?

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.180
The trailer only reveals the warlord for the
briefest of moments, walking on the farm he

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.360
appears to have retired to just like he did
in the comics.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.560
But what the comics don't tell us is what's
going to happen next.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.120
Is Thanos simply done?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.320
Or is there a second phase to his plan?

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.899
Does he know the surviving Avengers are coming
for him, or does he not see them as a threat?

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.000
Also why farming?

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.010
Does he just really like Stardew Valley?

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.040
The mind boggles.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.880
One of the biggest questions swirling around
Endgame is just when the story will be picking

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:58.380
up.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.700
One long-standing theory is that the movie
will begin after a time skip, picking up somewhere

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.600
in the vicinity of five years after the events
of Infinity War.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.420
But the first Endgame trailer neither confirms
nor denies this theory, leaving the time period

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.160
ambiguous.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.280
Some parts of the trailer, such as Tony Stark's
doomed jaunt through outer space, feel as

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:18.700
though they could be taking place within days
of the end of Infinity War.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.890
Other parts, such as the reveal of the samurai
Clint Barton, feel like they could be years

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.680
down the line.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.920
It's to the trailer's credit that we can't
decipher just when these things take place.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:31.700
Both options are probably true, there may
well be a time jump, but it doesn't need to

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.780
happen immediately.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.800
Right now, there's no way of being sure when
this movie is taking place.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.840
"What year is it?"

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.880
The Avengers' initial plan of attack against
Thanos was actually going pretty good until

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.740
Peter Quill lost it and went rogue…

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.980
Thanks Star Lord…

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.850
Although it is worth noting that Team Titan
barely drew a draw a drop of blood off Thanos,

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:53.120
and he did whip Hulk with only one lousy infinity
stone.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.020
So if brute force isn't going to win, what
will?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.520
The Endgame trailer ramps up to a short exchange
between Captain America and Black Widow.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.639
As Cap regards a picture of Peggy Carter,
the two superheroes discuss their upcoming

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.580
last-ditch plan.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:07.840
Just what are these two preparing to go do?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.900
And what does Peggy have to do with it?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.580
The hot rumor that's been running around for
months now, based on leaks from the movie's

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.150
production, is that the Avengers will use
time travel to turn back the clock on their

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.640
catastrophic defeat to somehow change Infinity
War's outcome.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.010
Whatever they're doing, we hope it corresponds
with Dr. Strange's mysterious plan.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.250
Remember, out of millions of possible outcomes,
he only saw one way to victory.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.060
Let's hope the survivors see it too.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:31.820
"How many we win?"

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:37.800
"One."

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.060
After the exhausting Infinity War, we wouldn't
blame you for sitting out on Ant-Man and the

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:43.560
Wasp.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.680
But those who skipped out also missed out
on a major cliffhanger one that the Endgame

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.700
trailer does away with in surprisingly casual
fashion.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.570
In the after-credits scene for Ant-Man and
the Wasp, Scott Lang's Ant-Man uses some Hank

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.350
Pym technology in the back of his van to transport
himself to the Quantum Realm, the under-explored

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.940
micro-dimension of the MCU.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.300
It's a uniquely dangerous domain, one that
the original Wasp was trapped in for years

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.740
before finally being rescued by Scott, Hank,
and Hope van Dyne.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.940
As it turned out, Scott's jaunt into the Quantum
Realm took place at the exact same time as

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.210
Thanos' snap, leaving his partners on the
outside dusted and him stuck inside with no

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.220
obvious way out.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.320
So it was a surprise to see Scott turn up
in the Endgame trailer acting as though nothing

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.320
had happened.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.320
How did he get out?

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.410
Did he use one of those "time vortexes" that
Janet warned him about?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.620
If so, what year did he end up in when he
left?

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.260
There’s this weird little detail hidden
right in front of our faces - if you look

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.010
really hard at the surveillance of Ant-Man
waving at the camera, it almost looks like

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.340
it says “1983”.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.540
Did he pop out 35 years too soon?

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.080
And what about Natasha saying “it’s the
front door.”

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.900
Is this just a tricky edit?

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:45.880
hmmmm.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.540
The ending of Avengers: Infinity War had some
tragic turns for everybody.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.140
Poor Scarlet Witch had to watch her beloved
Vision die not once, but twice, and the first

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.209
time, she was the one who had to kill him.

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:01.050
When Cap lost Bucky, he lost both his best
friend, and his greatest link to the past.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.140
But Rocket lost everything.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.900
It was jaw-dropping to see how easy it was
for Thanos to wipe out all the Guardians of

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.640
the Galaxy.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.370
We have to wonder if there's some reason why
Rocket was the only member of the team to

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.320
make it out alive.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.780
Not only is Rocket still kicking, but last
we saw him, he was stuck on Earth, which is

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.040
not the most fulfilling place to be when you
look like a filthy raccoon.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.209
"What's a raccoon?"

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:22.380
"What's a racoon?

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.760
It's what you are, stupid."

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.919
Has he taken up a permanent place at some
barstool south of Wakanda ? Or has he spent

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:29.499
all this time building bombs?

00:04:29.499 --> 00:04:33.340
Either way, the trailer gives us no hints
as to what he might be up to since Thanos

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.340
killed all his friends.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.509
The man formerly known as Hawkeye has been
missing in action for what feels like an eternity

00:04:39.509 --> 00:04:42.830
but now he's back with a new name and an apparent
thirst for blood.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.480
"Clearly retirement doesn't suit you.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.620
Got tired of shooting golf?"

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.820
The trailer for Endgame seems to confirm all
the rumors that Clint Barton will be taking

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.780
up the mantle of Ronin for the fourth Avengers
adventure, trading in his bow and arrow for

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.280
the sword of a roaming samurai.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.080
But one thing it didn't confirm is what he's
actually doing out there in Japan with that

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.200
new costume of his.

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:05.080
We can suppose with some confidence that Thanos'
decimation killed off Clint's whole family.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.640
Why else would he have gone so nuts?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.280
It's rumored that Clint is in the land of
the rising sun fighting the Yakuza, which

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.580
is cool if true, even if it is somewhat out
of nowhere.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:17.879
Other rumors further indicate that the Yakuza
he's fighting aren't human people, but instead

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.820
alien Skrulls, a tantalizing, if totally unproven
possibility.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.110
If he is killing Skrulls, how did he know
they were here on Earth?

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.600
Also, who is he working for, if anyone?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.980
Aliens or no aliens, what is the goal of this
lonely warrior?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.680
We don't know, but we've missed you, Hawkeye.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.430
We know you would've gone for the head.

